# LeakSanitizer suppressions for this test alone (its driver passes the file
# in LSAN_OPTIONS for the run of its own program, nothing else).
#
# CPython does not give back its own allocations at Py_Finalize: interned
# objects, type caches and arenas outlive the interpreter by design, so
# every program that embeds it leaks them, Aether's or not. A suppression
# matches any frame of an allocation's stack, so this is as tight as
# LeakSanitizer allows: what is reported with a libpython frame (CPython's
# own, and anything allocated inside a call that came through it) is
# dropped, and every other allocation of the harness, the runtime and the
# Aether code it calls is still checked.
leak:libpython
